      "heading": "B — Audience",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience, Section Eleven Lane use and passing\n\nThe audience is first-time, never-licensed applicants preparing for the West Virginia Class E knowledge examination, reading at a plain-English level with no prior driving knowledge assumed. Section Eleven teaches how to change lanes and pass safely, where passing is forbidden, and who yields to whom. It depends on the turning chapter for the three-to-four second rule and on the signals and markings chapter for the solid yellow line and signal rules. The rules progress from lane changes, through the passing procedure and its prohibitions, to the right-of-way situations.\n",
